title: 'bandersnatch: z=0-safe projective FFI codec for mul/msm host calls'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Route the `ed_on_bls12_381_bandersnatch_mul` and
    `ed_on_bls12_381_bandersnatch_msm` host calls through a new
    `bandersnatch_codec` that can round-trip the `z = 0` exceptional
    projective states HWCD arithmetic can produce on inputs outside the
    prime-order subgroup (e.g. anything from
    `deserialize_with_mode(.., Validate::No)`).

    The previous implementation hit `z.inverse().unwrap()` inside arkworks'
    `From<Projective> for Affine` and panicked before the bytes ever
    crossed the FFI. The host functions now use a 64-byte wire format that
    reuses the spare top bit of each `Fq` slot (`MODULUS_BIT_SIZE = 255`)
    as a 2-bit tag for the three `z = 0` exception shapes; the normal `z != 0`
    row is byte-identical to arkworks' uncompressed affine encoding, so
    well-behaved subgroup inputs remain wire-compatible.
crates:
- name: sp-crypto-ec-utils
  bump: minor
